From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:19:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/32] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: allow 32-bit capture

Playback front ends accept S32_LE, capture front ends only S16_LE and
S24_LE. S24_LE is described to the DSP with 24 bits per sample, i.e. as
packed 24-bit data, while ALSA's S24_LE carries the sample in a 32-bit
word, so a 24-bit recording cannot be taken through it. Allow S32_LE on
capture as well: bit width and container are then both 32 bits, and the
DSP converts its 24-bit codec samples into it. The topology still
decides which formats a front end offers.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
index e01d82ca718b..9002acf0e0cd 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -202,7 +202,8 @@ static const struct snd_pcm_hardware q6apm_dai_hardware_capture = {
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_PAUSE | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_RESUME |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_NO_REWINDS | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH),
-	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE),
+	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
+				 SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE),
 	.rates =                SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_48000,
 	.rate_min =             8000,
 	.rate_max =             48000,
